   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: COVID-19 vaccines efficiently and effectively delivered. 
Indicator: At least 150 million doses of COVID-19 vaccines procured and delivered to the country (OP1.1.2) 
Progress/Status: 241.97M doses of COVID-19 vaccines have been delivered to the country; 85.6M doses (35.39%) were financed under HEAL2. No vaccines have been procured under HEAL2 AF yet. DOH informed ADB that it is proposing to cancel HEAL2 AF and the uncommitted balance of HEAL2. 
Data Source: DOH updates, project survey and project progress report, data from VIMS. 
Baseline year: 2020 
Baseline value: 0 
Target year: 2024 
Target value: 150 million</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: COVID-19 vaccines efficiently and effectively delivered. 
Indicator: Gender- and socially inclusive protocol and guidelines on the deployment and administration of vaccines, addressing the specific needs of marginalized women and women in especially difficult circumstances, developed, approved, and disseminated (OP2.3.2) 
Progress/Status: Advisory No. 75 &amp;quot;Vaccination of Pregnant Women with COVID-19 vaccines&amp;quot; was approved on 20 August 2021 to prioritize pregnant women for COVID-19 vaccination. Advisory No.84 &amp;quot;Vaccination of Priority Group A Nationwide&#x201d; was approved on 6 September 2021. This was to prioritize Group A population (estimated at 24.7 million or 23% of the total population) as the first target group for COVID-19 vaccination. Group A includes prioritizes frontline health workers, people with comorbidities, pregnant women, indigent older persons, remaining older persons and indigent populations, and uniformed personnel. Furthermore, Advisory No. 127 &#x201c;Guidance on Vaccination of Booster Dose to Pregnant and Lactating Women&#x201d; was issued 31 January 2022 for booster shots for pregnant and lactating women. In order to reach out most marginalized women and vulnerable population (including people with disabilities, elderly who cannot access to vaccine site), DOH with support from WHO, USAID and ADB TA started community level demand generation and communication initiatives to ensure equity and inclusion in COVID-19 vaccination RESBAKUNA campaign in selected regions. This will continue until March 2023. 
Data Source: DOH updates, project survey and project progress report, data from VIMS. 
Baseline year: 2020 
Baseline value: N 
Baseline year: 2020 
Baseline value: N 
Target year: 2024 
Target value: Y</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
